    "final_message": "Here's what I found in Paris (ratings + prices), along with my picks:\n\n## 🏨 Hotel — **Montmartre Suites**\n| Hotel | Rating | Price/night |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Montmartre Suites** ✅ | 4.7 | **$110 – $200** |\n| Le Marais Boutique | 4.2 | $120 – $180 |\n| Good Night | 5.0 | $240 – $400 |\n| Luxury Palace | 5.0 | $500 – $1000 |\n\n*Best value: nearly the top rating, but the cheapest room in town (the 5.0‑rated hotels cost 2–10× more).*\n\n## 🚗 Car Rental — **Paris Rent-a-Car**\n| Company | Rating | Price/day |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Paris Rent-a-Car** ✅ | 4.5 | **$45** |\n| Eiffel Tower Car Rental | 5.0 | $60 |\n\n*Top-rated option is 33% more expensive (its own reviewers call it \"a bit pricey\"), so Paris Rent-a-Car is the smart budget pick — near-perfect score, convenient spot by the Louvre.*\n\n## 🍽️ Restaurant — **Le Baratin**\n| Restaurant | Rating | Price/person |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Le Baratin** ✅ | **4.8** (highest in Paris) | $30 |\n| New Asiaway | 4.6 | $30 |\n| New Israeli Restaurant | 4.5 | $20 |\n| China Garden / Chez L'Ami Jean | 4.4 | — |\n\n*Highest-rated restaurant in the city at a standard bistro price (note: cash only!).*\n\n---\n\n## 💰 Minimum cost for a 3-day trip\n| Item | Calculation | Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hotel (Montmartre Suites) | $110 × 3 nights | $330 |\n| Car rental (Paris Rent-a-Car) | $45 × 3 days | $135 |\n| Restaurant (Le Baratin, 2 meals/day) | $30 × 6 meals | $180 |\n| **Total** | | **$645** |\n\n💡 If you want to squeeze the budget further, swap Le Baratin for the New Israeli Rest",
